{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794083224,"nonce":"d5rLiSjozx+pNJTUD7UkhZ2QxfI=","message":"Root cause. On web the motion key includes a call-site index (builtin.rs:112:17:\u003cn\u003e) that drifts upward on every subtree rebuild, so each show got a fresh key and animated by accident; the previous key was never cleaned up. The web frame loop ran initialize_motion_animations and end_stable_motion_frame only on rebuilds and never began a motion frame, so an unmounted motion never exited or dropped. A theme switch rebuilds the tree and resets the call counters to 0, which reuses a key whose stale state is Visible, so start_stable_motion keeps it and the entrance never replays. Fix (uncommitted, crates/blinc_app/src/web.rs): begin the motion frame before each initialize on the rebuild paths, and mark and close the frame every frame when nothing rebuilds, as the windowed loop does. Verified on a local build of the catalog site: the entrance plays on every show before and after Expressive, Restrained and Hybrid. New test web/components/tests/motion_theme_browser.py fails against the live site and passes against the fixed build. The calendar, selection-styles, component-styles, gallery (71 pages) and charts browser suites pass on the fixed build.","files":null}]}